content.text:
Finding submitted.

**Summary:** Section 6.1 is a **deviation** (high severity). It binds us — the Company — not to participate in any project similar to the Site with respect to Deerskin Products "or products substantially similar," extending to unnamed "companies similar to Wilson's House of Leather and Excelled," and it also grants HDI an exclusive right over our own "Deerskin" brand.

It fails the fallback on several material terms:
- scope is open-ended rather than a single named competing product;
- no 12-month cap (the term auto-renews annually under Section 4.1, so the restriction can run indefinitely);
- no carve-out for our internal development or for acquisitions;
- HDI's retained exclusivity over our own brand is itself a field-of-use restriction.

Redline (validated, preferred level): Section 6.1 is converted into an express permission for the Company to participate in such projects and confirms HDI has no exclusive right to the "Deerskin" brand. Section 6.3, which restricts HDI, is left untouched because it benefits us, and the HDI trademark licence in the following paragraphs (non-exclusive) is preserved. The Section 9(b) Globix proviso is noted as a sourcing/exclusivity condition, not flagged here.
